export abstract anchor Type as type:
    whatIsAType:
        A type describes what kind of value something is. It defines which
        values are allowed, which operations they support, and where they can be
        used.

        // TODO: This might be too much information here.
        The compiler uses types to check whether expressions and assignments
        make sense. Each expression produces a value of a particular type, which
        may be explicitly declared or inferred by the compiler. When a value is
        used where its type is not allowed, the compiler reports a type error.

    description:: simple:: complex
